WEBVTT

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:41.990
Fill 'er up!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:01.540
We Don't Care What You Think

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.030
Hey! What the...

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.070
Thief!

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.110
Stop, thief!

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.580
Is something wrong?

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.680
Somebody stole his truck.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.450
That one.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.220
- Come in, station. This is...
- Um, that's okay.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.730
No it's not! Your truck's been stolen!

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.270
Never mind.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.730
I-It's okay. Don't worry about it.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.830
Hey! Hold it!

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.430
Hey!

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.310
Hold it!

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.340
Shit! Let go! Get off me, pig!

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.880
One of those bad elements, huh?

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.550
Hello, Takasaki Police Department.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.250
This is Assistant Inspector Shinobu Nagumo...

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:08.430
National Safety Week

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.260
with the Tokyo Metro Police's SV2.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.770
I'd like to speak to Goto.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.990
Mr. Goto?

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.270
Our Second Unit is supposed to be there...

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.240
as part of your centennial celebration.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.710
And so, our hypothesis is that the target...

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.420
is currently heading north on the Kan'etsu Expressway.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:29.090
This is the one? That unbelievable case where a thief...

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.930
stole a cargo trailer that had already been stolen?

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.030
According to the statement we got...

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.630
from that Beach House sympathizer we arrested, yes.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.730
Now I've seen everything.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.310
But what makes you think that the thief...

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.140
is going north on the Kan'etsu, Captain?

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.740
Because there's no sign that he's gotten off it.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.080
Don't you know that if you close off the exits...

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.980
a highway is like the room in a locked-room case?

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:58.220
It's what's <i>in</i> the containers that worries me, though.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.660
It's a demo Labor that was scheduled to be shown...

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.920
at the International Labor Show at Harumi three days from now...

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.730
but it was stolen <i>the first</i> time right after...

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.860
it arrived from West Germany last weekend.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.370
Captain Nagumo is working on what happened after that...

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:16.410
but the manufacturer's being tight- lipped and hasn't told us much.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:18.240
Who cares what happened?

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:21.180
All we have to do is stop it and take back the container, right?

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.050
I'm hoping that it's not...

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.610
gonna turn out to be a jack-in-the-box when we open it.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.180
But I have a feeling it will.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.880
Fujioka Exit
\h
\h
\h
\h
\h
\h
\h
\h
\h


00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.840
Huh? They have a checkpoint set up over there!

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.480
Can I speak to the person in charge here?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.040
That's me. I'm Gunma Prefecture Police Superintendent Kusumoto.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.520
Wow, the Superintendent came out to personally take charge?

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.180
That's amazing.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.120
And your response time is excellent.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:45.890
Well, I can't let regional police get a bad reputation.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.400
This is really great.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:53.740
But do you think you could take down the checkpoint right away?

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.210
What?

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.400
We don't want the thief to get off the highway.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:01.040
So we don't want to make him nervous with checkpoints like this.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.340
B-But...

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:04.680
Let's just assume for the moment...

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:08.190
that he's carrying something very dangerous in that container.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.350
This is, mind you, highly probable.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:16.230
What if he sees the checkpoint and uses it here in desperation?

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:20.490
Or what if he forces his way past you and uses it in town?

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.030
What would you do?

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.600
Report from the Fujioka Interchange!

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:29.160
A semi that they believe to be the target has just left the highway!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.710
- What?
- Oops.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.690
This is GP2 Haruna.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.730
Target spotted. Now pursuing.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.630
The Foreign Affairs Section?

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:00.540
It looks like they were planning to smuggle the stolen container...

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.130
into the Communist bloc to raise operating funds.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.480
Ah. Which is why Foreign Affairs is getting involved.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:12.150
Chief Kaiho is wound up, trying to score points with this.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:15.750
Try to rein him in, okay?

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.620
Could you hang on for a second?

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.430
Yes?

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.190
Everything is set up as you instructed.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.270
Do all you can to catch the criminal before he leaves the prefecture.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:31.570
- We're counting on you.
- Yes, sir. We'll get right after him.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.110
Where was I?

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.970
Never mind about the Chief, though.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.480
Where do you think the first thief would have gone...

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.110
if it weren't for the second theft?

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.050
Niigata Harbor, maybe.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.750
Bingo.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.810
But still...

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:57.060
What are the chances that some other group set up the first thief?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.930
None, I'd say.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:04.060
Anyway, I don't have the slightest idea <i>why</i> he's driving that truck.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.940
This is GP2 Haruna.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.980
Target has gotten back onto the Kan'etsu at the Maebashi IC.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.980
Roger. Stay on him.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:22.510
Chief command car here. All cars, report in.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.220
Kannagawa, ready!

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.850
Kaburagawa, ready!

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.430
Yamagawa, ready!

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:28.720
Torikawa, ready!

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:36.070
The target's just a few kilometers behind us, right?

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:38.500
How come we're going to all this trouble?

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:42.560
We can't get civilian traffic involved, you moron.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.840
Geez, you're starting to think like Ota!

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.750
Don't say that!

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.340
What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.590
Where are we now?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.220
Hey, Asanuma! Do you hear me?

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.100
Move along! There's nothing to see here!

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:28.510
So there's no chance he'll leave the highway before he reaches us?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.320
His side-trip to Fujioka not withstanding...

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.950
considering that he got back onto a high-risk road like the highway...

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:38.260
it's safe to assume that he's heading someplace far away...

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.230
probably towards Niigata.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:43.360
But what if there was some slip-up...

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:47.460
and he's really trying to make it past Mikuni Pass?

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.700
You sure worry a lot.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.640
It's gotten me where I am today.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.710
So you look before you make others leap, huh?

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:02.580
Two unidentified Labors have been spotted at Mikuni Pass!

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:03.680
What?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.950
We're after a semi, right?

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.640
You crazy bastard!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.980
Make sure you stop him, okay, Izumi?

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.880
Just leave it to me!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.220
Here it comes!

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:00.710
No way!

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.370
I don't get it.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:04.610
Why?

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:08.050
Sure, I stole the truck, but how come...

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.590
they're making such a big deal about it?

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.520
Pin the container!

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.360
What're you doing, Noa?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.310
Get out of my way, Izumi!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.000
You're in <i>my</i> way, Ota!

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.010
- Fight later!
- Yeah!

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:46.780
Okay, criminal!

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.320
- Izumi! Get on the trailer!
- Roger!

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.290
Unit 2! Get back onto the trailer! We're going after him!

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.380
Gotcha!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:25.760
Shit!

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.900
I <i>knew</i> that was no ordinary container.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.050
Who the hell are <i>you</i>?

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:51.050
Who am I? Who are <i>you</i>?

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.220
It's foolish to give your name when asked...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.090
but when they talk about Yu'ichi Moritomo, code-named...

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.130
"The Wrath of the South Seas," member of the Beach House...

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:02.630
sympathizer group, the " Earth Defense Force Independents..."

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.640
they're talking about <i>me</i>.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.710
What happened to Comrade Asanuma?

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:07.970
I don't know!

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.130
Are you a new contact?

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:14.740
I'm just a seasonal worker who stole the truck on impulse!

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:18.310
A seasonal worker?

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:25.360
Then you're one of us!

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.920
Another helpless victim of the government's twisted policies!

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.430
No, l...

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.160
Let's fight side by side!

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.670
Our dawn is fast approaching!

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:36.740
Um... that's west.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:42.930
An archive container works on the same principle as a...

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:48.240
computer file archive: it stores a Labor by compressing its volume.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.810
If you knew that, why didn't you <i>tell</i> us?

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:55.650
Until that Labor's arm popped out, I completely forgot about it.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.090
And you're a <i>cop</i>?

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.060
You've got room to talk.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.530
Cut it out, you two.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.660
- This is partly <i>your</i> fault, Noa!
- What?

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:10.960
Yeah! If you had moved faster, we could've pinned down the container!

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:12.330
But...

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:16.770
It's a good thing the container was set to send out a signal...

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:20.870
when it activated, because if it <i>hadn't</i>, we'd have lost it by now!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:24.920
If Ota hadn't blocked the road, we could've chased after it!

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:26.210
Right?

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.680
Um... I suppose.

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.590
- See?
- What?

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:34.930
Anyway, that happens because you're never paying attention!

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:36.590
Yeah, tell him! Tell him!

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:38.600
Shinohara, you son of a...

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:40.430
- What's <i>your</i> problem?
- Ota, the way you...

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:10.630
Good work. What's the target's status?

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:12.620
Right this way.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:16.370
Heading north on National Highway 17.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.700
It's managed to outdistance us.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:23.900
This may be sudden, but the Second Unit will now coordinate with SEE.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:27.910
Shaft Enterprises Europe? That thing's manufacturer?

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.850
So is this to be a joint operation between Industry and the police?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.780
They felt partly responsible for having caused a scandal...

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.050
so they asked to help.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.090
And seeing as how one of our Labors is looking like <i>that</i>...

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:41.420
I don't see any reason for you to turn them down.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:44.430
I have a meeting in the morning, so I have to go.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:47.330
Don't let me down, Goto.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.600
Some Labors have gotten past Mikuni Pass.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.070
SEE is acting independently?

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:34.180
If they set up a joint operation, they justify their actions, right?

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:38.740
I think what they're really trying to do is destroy evidence.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:43.310
I mean, what was in that container was smuggled into the country...

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:46.150
by SEE under the pretext of the International Labor Show.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:49.230
The Type-7 Brocken is a bona fide military Labor.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.690
It's not something that a civilian organization...

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.770
can just waltz into the country with.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:17:02.290
Muika Interchange
\h
